+# Enterprise acceptance instructions
+
+1) Create ops/runbooks/prefilled_values.env from docs/runbooks/prefilled_values.template and fill with your environment values.
+2) Ensure required images are built and pushed to CONTAINER_REGISTRY (prompt-registry, aegis-fl images).
+3) Ensure COSIGN_KMS_URI, REKOR_SERVER, S3_UPLOAD are set and accessible by CI/ops.
+4) Run the one-click test locally or via GitHub Actions:
+   - Locally: source ops/runbooks/prefilled_values.env && bash ops/runbooks/enterprise_acceptance_oneclick.sh
+   - CI: dispatch .github/workflows/enterprise_acceptance.yml
+5) After run completes, inspect the produced auditor bundle under /tmp and upload to your auditor or S3.
+
+Notes:
+- The Opacus client example requires GPUs or PyTorch CPU fallback. Adjust training loop to use your model and dataset.
+- Secure aggregation example is illustrative only — do NOT rely on it for production confidentiality without using a proven library.
